          {
            "id": "block-33-6-sol",
            "type": "text",
            "content": "解答\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\because \\frac{d\\left(\\sin x^2\\right)}{d(\\sqrt{x})}=\\frac{2 x \\cos x^2 d x}{\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{x}} d x}=4 x \\sqrt{x} \\cos x^2 \\\\\n& \\therefore d\\left(\\sin x^2\\right)=\\left(4 x \\sqrt{x} \\cos x^2\\right) d(\\sqrt{x}) \\\\\n& d\\left(\\frac{e^{2 x}}{x^2}\\right)=\\frac{x^2 d\\left(e^{2 x}\\right)-e^{2 x} d x^2}{\\left(x^2\\right)^2}=\\frac{x^2 e^{2 x} 2 d x-e^{2 x} 2 x d x}{\\left(x^2\\right)^2}=\\frac{2 e^{2 x}(x-1)}{x^3} d x \\\\\n& d\\left(\\frac{1}{\\omega} \\sin \\omega x+1\\right)=\\frac{1}{\\omega}(\\sin \\omega x)^{\\prime} d x=\\cos \\omega x d x \\\\\n& d\\left[\\ln \\left(x+\\sqrt{x^2+1}\\right)\\right]=\\frac{1}{x+\\sqrt{x^2+1}} d\\left(x+\\sqrt{x^2+1}\\right) \\\\\n& =\\frac{1}{x+\\sqrt{x^2+1}}\\left(1+\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x^2+1}}\\right) d x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x^2+1}} d x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
          }
